    "scenario": "BGP Attribute AS Path",
    "goals": "• Configure EBGP between router {{router2_name}} and {{router4_name}}.\n  AS {{as1}}: {{router1_name}}, {{router2_name}}, {{router3_name}}\n  AS {{as2}}: {{router4_name}}\n• Configure EBGP between router {{router3_name}} and {{router4_name}}.\n• Configure IBGP between all routers in AS {{as1}} using their loopback0 addresses.\n• Advertise the {{router4_loopback0_network}} /{{router4_loopback0_prefix_len}} network on router {{router4_name}}.\n• Using only the AS Path attribute, make router {{router1_name}} prefer the path learned through router {{router3_name}} for traffic to {{router4_loopback0_network}} /{{router4_loopback0_prefix_len}}. Do this by making the AS path advertised from router {{router4_name}} to router {{router2_name}} longer than the path advertised from router {{router4_name}} to router {{router3_name}}.",
